Thought: The proton NMR spectra for the compound "CCC(C)(C)C(C1=CC=CC=C1)OOCC2CCCC2" shows signals at 2.22 ppm, 2.32 ppm, 4.46 ppm, and 7.06 ppm. These signals need to be compared with typical chemical shifts for similar structures to confirm the identity of the compound. I will retrieve the typical proton chemical shifts for hydrocarbons to validate these shifts.
